            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "I don't this is reasonably possible with your code right now.\r\n\r\nI would suggest investigating at least these options:\r\n- Load whole 'mini.nvim' without lazy loading. This will have hardly any impact on startup speed. Inside its config you can set up 'mini.colors' right away and manually lazy load others with autocommands. Something like `vim.api.nvim_create_autocmd('InsertEnter', { once = true, callback = function() <your code goes here> end })`.\r\n- Use standalone modules for more granular setup.",
